  {
   "id": "q014",
   "question": "what are the steps in combat and when do I have priority as the defending player?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 1704,
    "completion_tokens": 625,
    "total_tokens": 2329,
    "cost": 0.000261252,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000261252,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000148752,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.0001125
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "The combat phase consists of five steps in order: beginning of combat, declare attackers, declare blockers, combat damage, and end of combat ([506.1]). The declare blockers and combat damage steps are skipped if no creatures are declared as attackers ([506.1]). If any creature has first strike or double strike, there are two combat damage steps ([506.1]).\n\nAs the defending player, you receive priority at the beginning of most steps and phases, after any turn-based actions and triggered abilities have been dealt with ([117.3a]). Specifically:\n- **Beginning of combat step**: After the turn-based action of choosing a defending player (if applicable, [507.1]) and any beginning-of-combat triggers resolve, the active player gets priority first ([117.3a]). You (the defending player) will get priority later in this step after the active player passes.\n- **Declare attackers step**: After attackers are declared and any triggers resolve, the active player gets priority first ([117.3a]). You get priority after the active player passes.\n- **Declare blockers step**: After blockers are declared and any triggers resolve, the active player gets priority first ([117.3a]). You get priority after the active player passes.\n- **Combat damage step**: Combat damage is assigned and dealt simultaneously as a turn-based action without the stack ([510.1], [510.2]). After damage is dealt and any triggers are put on the stack, the active player gets priority first ([117.3a]). You get priority after the active player passes.\n- **End of combat step**: The active player gets priority first as soon as the step begins ([511.1], [117.3a]). You get priority after the active player passes.\n\nIn a multiplayer game where all opponents are defending players (e.g., the Attack Multiple Players option), the same priority order applies: the active player (attacking player) gets priority first in each step, then the defending players in turn order ([802.2], [117.3a]). In the shared team turns option, the active team gets priority first ([805.10f]).",
   "citations": [
    "506.1",
    "117.3a",
    "507.1",
    "510.1",
    "510.2",
    "511.1",
    "802.2",
    "805.10f"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  },
