  {
   "id": "q021",
   "question": "what happens during the cleanup step?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 1728,
    "completion_tokens": 513,
    "total_tokens": 2241,
    "cost": 0.000243252,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000243252,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000150912,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 9.234e-05
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "During the cleanup step, the following occurs in order:\n\n1. **Turn-based actions** (rule [703.4p]): Immediately after the active player discards to hand size (if necessary), all damage is removed from permanents and all “until end of turn” and “this turn” effects end. These happen simultaneously and do not use the stack.\n\n2. **State-based actions check** (rule [704.3]): The game checks for state-based actions. If any are performed, the check repeats until none are performed. Then any triggered abilities waiting to be put on the stack are put there.\n\n3. **Priority** (rule [514.3a]): Normally, no player gets priority during the cleanup step. However, if state-based actions were performed or triggered abilities are waiting (including those that trigger “at the beginning of the next cleanup step”), the active player gets priority. Players may then cast spells and activate abilities. Once the stack is empty and all players pass in succession, another cleanup step begins.\n\n4. **If an effect ends the turn** during the cleanup step (rule [724.1d]): A new cleanup step begins immediately.\n\nKey definitions: The cleanup step is the second and final step of the ending phase (per the Cleanup Step definition). It is a step where normally no player receives priority, except as described above (rule [500.3]).",
   "citations": [
    "514.3a",
    "704.3",
    "703.4p",
    "724.1d",
    "500.3",
