    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "After the active player casts a spell, the active player receives priority first. This is because rule [117.3c] states that if a player has priority when they cast a spell, that player receives priority afterward. The active player is the one who had priority before casting (as per [117.3a] and [509.2] for the combat phase, or similar rules for other phases), so they retain priority after the spell is cast. No other player gets priority before the active player does in this situation.",
