     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000166662,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 5.76e-05
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "Yes, you can activate mana abilities while a spell with split second is on the stack. Rule [702.61b] explicitly states that players may activate mana abilities while a spell with split second is on the stack. This is an exception to the general restriction imposed by split second (rule [702.61a]), which normally prevents players from casting other spells or activating non-mana abilities. Mana abilities are defined in rule [605.1] and follow special rules: they don’t use the stack (rule [605.3b]) and can be activated even without priority in certain circumstances (rule [117.1d]). During the resolution of a spell or ability, players may also activate mana abilities when a cost requires mana (rule [608.2g]). Therefore, the presence of a split second spell does not prevent you from activating mana abilities.",
   "citations": [
    "702.61b",
    "702.61a",
    "605.1",
    "605.3b",
    "117.1d",
    "608.2g"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  },
  {
   "id": "c001",
   "question": "[Counterspell] is on top of the stack targeting my [Divination]. When everyone passes priority, what resolves first, and does Divination still resolve?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 2218,
    "completion_tokens": 307,
    "total_tokens": 2525,
    "cost": 0.000250272,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000250272,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000195012,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 5.526e-05
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "Counterspell resolves first, and Divination does not resolve. When all players pass priority, the top object on the stack—Counterspell—resolves ([608.1]). Counterspell's effect counters target spell ([Counterspell card text]), which means the targeted Divination is removed from the stack and put into its owner's graveyard without resolving ([701.6a], [112.1]). Divination never gets to resolve because it is countered before it would be the top object on the stack. The stack is a zone where spells exist as objects; Counterspell is a spell on the stack ([112.1]), and it resolves first because it is on top ([117.7]). After Counterspell resolves, Divination is countered and no longer on the stack, so it cannot resolve later.",
   "citations": [
    "608.1",
    "701.6a",
    "112.1",
    "117.7",
    "Counterspell card text"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  },
  {
   "id": "c002",
   "question": "My [Charging Rhino] has trample and is blocked by [Vampire Nighthawk], which has deathtouch. How much combat damage do I have to assign to the blocker before I can trample the rest over to the player?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 2200,
    "completion_tokens": 318,
    "total_tokens": 2518,
    "cost": 0.000250632,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000250632,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000193392,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 5.724e-05
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "You must assign at least 1 damage to Vampire Nighthawk (the blocker) before you can assign any excess damage to the defending player. This is because deathtouch makes any nonzero amount of combat damage lethal for the purpose of determining excess damage (rule [702.2c]), and trample requires that all blocking creatures be assigned lethal damage before excess damage can be assigned to the defending player (rule [702.19b]). Since Vampire Nighthawk has deathtouch, 1 damage is lethal, so you assign 1 damage to it and the remaining 3 damage (from Charging Rhino’s 4 power) to the defending player.",
   "citations": [
    "702.2c",
    "702.19b",
    "Lethal Damage",
    "Excess Damage"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  },
  {
   "id": "c003",
   "question": "I have [Monastery Swiftspear] on the battlefield and I cast [Shardless Agent]. When its cascade ability puts a noncreature spell onto the stack, does Monastery Swiftspear's prowess trigger before or after that cascaded spell resolves?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 2468,
    "completion_tokens": 602,
    "total_tokens": 3070,
    "cost": 0.000325872,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000325872,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000217512,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.00010836
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "Monastery Swiftspear's prowess triggers **after** the cascaded spell is put onto the stack, but **before** that cascaded spell resolves. Here's the detailed sequence:\n\n1. You cast Shardless Agent. Its cascade ability triggers (rule 702.85a).\n2. Cascade resolves: you exile cards until you exile a nonland card with lesser mana value, then you may cast that card without paying its mana cost (rule 702.85a). Casting that card during resolution follows the steps in 601.2a–i, and no player gets priority after it's cast (rule 608.2g). The cascaded spell becomes the topmost object on the stack.\n3. **Prowess triggers** when you cast a noncreature spell (rule 702.108a). The trigger event (casting the cascaded spell) happens during the resolution of cascade. However, triggered abilities that trigger during resolution are put onto the stack only after the current spell or ability finishes resolving (rule 608.2p). So prowess triggers now but does not go on the stack yet.\n4. Cascade finishes resolving. Then, after Shardless Agent's cascade ability has fully resolved, the prowess trigger is put onto the stack (rule 608.2p).\n5. The prowess trigger resolves before the cascaded spell, because prowess goes on the stack on top of the spell that caused it to trigger (Monastery Swiftspear ruling #2).\n\nThus, Monastery Swiftspear gets +1/+1 from prowess **before** the cascaded noncreature spell resolves, but **after** that spell has been put onto the stack.\n\nKey rules: [702.108a] (prowess definition), [702.85a] (cascade definition), [608.2g] (casting during resolution), [608.2p] (triggered abilities during resolution), [Monastery Swiftspear ruling #2] (prowess resolves before the spell that triggered it).",
   "citations": [
    "702.108a",
    "702.85a",
    "608.2g",
    "608.2p",
    "Monastery Swiftspear ruling #2"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  },
  {
   "id": "c004",
   "question": "My opponent's [Grizzly Bears] has 2 damage marked on it. Do state-based actions make it die before my [Lightning Bolt] resolves?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 1927,
