    "total_tokens": 2274,
    "cost": 0.000231282,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000231282,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000168822,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 6.246e-05
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "No, state-based actions do not make the Grizzly Bears die before Lightning Bolt resolves. State-based actions are checked only when a player would receive priority (rule 704.3), not during the resolution of a spell or ability (rule 704.4). Lightning Bolt is an instant that resolves as a spell; during its resolution, the 3 damage is dealt to the Grizzly Bears, which already has 2 damage marked on it. The total damage marked (5) exceeds its toughness (2), but state-based actions are not checked until after the spell finishes resolving and a player would next get priority (rule 117.2d, 405.6f). At that point, the creature is destroyed as a state-based action (rule 704.5g). The damage from Lightning Bolt and the pre-existing damage are both considered when state-based actions are checked after resolution.",
   "citations": [
    "704.3",
    "704.4",
    "704.5g",
    "117.2d",
    "405.6f",
    "120.5",
    "120.6",
    "302.7"
   ],
