   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "No, the exiled creature does not return to the battlefield. Banishing Light's one-shot effect that exiles the creature \"until this enchantment leaves the battlefield\" is waiting for Banishing Light to leave the battlefield. However, phasing out does not cause a permanent to leave the battlefield; it simply treats the permanent as though it doesn't exist while it's phased out. Rule [702.26d] states that phasing does not cause a permanent to change zones, and zone-change triggers (including leaves-the-battlefield triggers) do not trigger when a permanent phases out. Additionally, [Teferi's Protection ruling #21] explicitly says that any one-shot effects waiting \"until [this] leaves the battlefield,\" such as that of Banishing Light, won't happen when a permanent phases out. Therefore, the one-shot effect that would return the creature is not created, and the creature remains exiled indefinitely until Banishing Light actually leaves the battlefield (e.g., by being destroyed, exiled, or returned to hand).",
   "citations": [
    "702.26d",
    "Teferi's Protection ruling #21"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  },
