  {
   "id": "c015",
   "question": "[Grist, the Hunger Tide] is in my graveyard. Can I return it with [Animate Dead], and what happens?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 4096,
    "completion_tokens": 1188,
    "total_tokens": 5284,
    "cost": 0.000577872,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000577872,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000364032,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.00021384
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "Yes, you can return Grist, the Hunger Tide from your graveyard with Animate Dead. Here is the detailed sequence and outcome:\n\n1. **Animate Dead targets Grist in the graveyard.** Animate Dead is an Aura with \"Enchant creature card in a graveyard,\" so it targets a creature card in a graveyard when cast. Grist, the Hunger Tide is a creature card in the graveyard (per [Grist, the Hunger Tide ruling #1]: \"Anywhere but on the battlefield, Grist is a Legendary Planeswalker Creature — Grist Insect\").\n\n2. **Animate Dead enters the battlefield attached to Grist in the graveyard.** Rule [113.6m] notes that abilities of an Aura that specify moving the object it's on out of a particular zone function only in that zone; Animate Dead's triggered ability functions on the battlefield, but its enchant ability allows it to target a card in the graveyard. When Animate Dead enters, it is attached to Grist in the graveyard.\n\n3. **Animate Dead's triggered ability resolves.** The ability says: \"When this Aura enters, if it's on the battlefield, it loses 'enchant creature card in a graveyard' and gains 'enchant creature put onto the battlefield with this Aura.' Return enchanted creature card to the battlefield under your control and attach this Aura to it.\" Since Animate Dead is on the battlefield as the ability resolves (per [Animate Dead ruling #0]: \"If Animate Dead isn't on the battlefield as its triggered ability resolves, none of its effects happen\"), it returns Grist from the graveyard to the battlefield.\n\n4. **Grist enters the battlefield as a planeswalker, not a creature.** Per [Grist, the Hunger Tide ruling #1]: \"Once it enters the battlefield, it is no longer a creature and is just a planeswalker.\" So Grist enters as a legendary planeswalker (not a creature).\n\n5. **Animate Dead attempts to attach to Grist.** Animate Dead gains \"enchant creature put onto the battlefield with this Aura.\" However, Grist on the battlefield is not a creature — it is a planeswalker. Therefore, Animate Dead cannot legally enchant Grist. Per [Animate Dead ruling #4]: \"If the creature put onto the battlefield has protection from black—or if the creature can't legally be enchanted by Animate Dead for another reason—Animate Dead won't be able to attach to it. It will be put into the graveyard as a state-based action, causing its delayed triggered ability to trigger.\" Since Grist is not a creature, Animate Dead cannot attach to it. As a state-based action (rule [704.4] and [704.8]), Animate Dead is put into its owner's graveyard because it is an Aura not attached to a legal object or player.\n\n6. **Animate Dead's delayed triggered ability triggers.** Animate Dead has: \"When this Aura leaves the battlefield, that creature's controller sacrifices it.\" When Animate Dead is put into the graveyard, this ability triggers. However, \"that creature\" refers to the creature put onto the battlefield with Animate Dead — Grist. But Grist is a planeswalker, not a creature, so the sacrifice effect applies to Grist. The ability says \"that creature's controller sacrifices it.\" Since Grist is a permanent on the battlefield, its controller must sacrifice it (even though it's a planeswalker, the ability still targets the object that was returned). Grist is sacrificed and put into the graveyard.\n\n**Result:** Grist enters the battlefield briefly, then Animate Dead is put into the graveyard for failing to enchant a legal permanent, and Grist is sacrificed due to Animate Dead's leaves-the-battlefield trigger. Grist ends up back in the graveyard, and Animate Dead is in the graveyard as well.\n\n**Key rules relied on:** [113.6m] (abilities function in specific zones), [Grist, the Hunger Tide ruling #1] (Grist is a creature card in graveyard, not a creature on battlefield), [Animate Dead ruling #0] (Animate Dead must be on battlefield for its trigger to work), [Animate Dead ruling #4] (if Aura can't attach, it's put into graveyard and sacrifice trigger occurs), [704.4] and [704.8] (state-based actions check legality of Aura attachment).",
   "citations": [
    "113.6m",
    "Grist, the Hunger Tide ruling #1",
    "Animate Dead ruling #0",
    "Animate Dead ruling #4",
    "704.4",
    "704.8"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  },
  {
   "id": "c016",
   "question": "My commander [Skullbriar, the Walking Grave] has four +1/+1 counters on it. It dies, I move it to the command zone, then recast it. Does it keep the counters, and does [Doubling Season] double them as it re-enters?",
