    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "No, Skullbriar does not keep the counters when it is recast from the command zone, and Doubling Season does not double them as it enters. When Skullbriar moves from the command zone to the battlefield, it is a new object entering the battlefield (rule [400.10]). Counters are not retained when an object moves from one zone to another (rule [122.2]), so the four +1/+1 counters that were on Skullbriar in the command zone cease to exist. Skullbriar’s own ability that says “Counters remain on Skullbriar as it moves to any zone other than a player's hand or library” only applies when it moves *from* the battlefield *to* another zone (e.g., to the command zone when it dies), not when it moves from the command zone to the battlefield. Since Skullbriar enters the battlefield without any counters, Doubling Season’s replacement effect (which doubles counters that an effect would put on a permanent) has nothing to double. Doubling Season does affect permanents that enter with counters (Doubling Season ruling #2), but here no counters are being placed by any effect as Skullbriar enters, so it does not apply.",
   "citations": [
    "400.10",
    "122.2",
    "Skullbriar, the Walking Grave ruling #2",
    "Doubling Season ruling #2"
   ],
