  {
   "id": "c017",
   "question": "I cast [Final Fortune] to take an extra turn. During that extra turn I use [Sundial of the Infinite] to end the turn before the end step. Do I still lose the game?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 2389,
    "completion_tokens": 379,
    "total_tokens": 2768,
    "cost": 0.000278622,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000278622,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000210402,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 6.822e-05
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "No, you do not lose the game. Final Fortune creates a delayed triggered ability that triggers “at the beginning of that turn’s end step.” When you activate Sundial of the Infinite to end the turn before the end step, the end step is skipped entirely (rule [724.1e]). Because the end step never occurs, the delayed triggered ability never triggers, so you never lose the game. This is confirmed by the Final Fortune ruling: “If you end up skipping the extra turn that is gained, you do not lose the game” — here, you are skipping the end step of the extra turn, which prevents the loss condition from triggering. The Sundial ruling also states that “at the beginning of the end step”-triggered abilities won’t get the chance to trigger that turn because the end step is skipped, and those abilities will trigger at the beginning of the end step of the next turn. However, since Final Fortune’s ability is tied specifically to that extra turn’s end step, it will never trigger in a later turn, so the loss is avoided permanently.",
   "citations": [
    "724.1e",
    "Final Fortune ruling #1",
    "Sundial of the Infinite ruling #1"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  },
