     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "You choose what Clone copies as it enters the battlefield, not as it is cast. The choice is made when the replacement effect from Clone's ability applies to the event of it entering the battlefield. This choice does not use the stack and cannot be responded to by your opponent. Once Clone enters, it is already a copy of the chosen creature (or a 0/0 if you choose not to copy anything). Your opponent can only respond to the Clone spell while it is on the stack, before it resolves and enters the battlefield. This is based on rule [707.6], which states that choices for 'as [this] enters the battlefield' abilities are made when the object enters, and Clone's ability is such an ability. Additionally, Clone ruling #0 confirms the ability does not target, and Clone ruling #5 notes you can choose not to copy anything. The choice is part of the replacement effect that modifies how Clone enters, and replacement effects do not use the stack (see rule [616.1c] for how replacement effects are applied).",
   "citations": [
    "707.6",
    "Clone ruling #0",
    "Clone ruling #5",
