  {
   "id": "c019",
   "question": "I activate my [Flooded Strand]'s ability, then activate [Gogo, Master of Mimicry] with X=2 to copy it twice. How many lands do I get from that one Flooded Strand?",
   "served_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
   "provider": "DeepInfra",
   "temperature_sent": 0.0,
   "seed_sent": 42,
   "usage": {
    "prompt_tokens": 4500,
    "completion_tokens": 796,
    "total_tokens": 5296,
    "cost": 0.000543672,
    "is_byok": false,
    "prompt_tokens_details": {
     "cached_tokens": 64,
     "cache_write_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0,
     "video_tokens": 0
    },
    "cost_details": {
     "upstream_inference_cost": 0.000543672,
     "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000400392,
     "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.00014328
    },
    "completion_tokens_details": {
     "reasoning_tokens": 0,
     "image_tokens": 0,
     "audio_tokens": 0
    }
   },
   "answered": true,
   "text": "You get three lands total from that one Flooded Strand activation. Here's the step-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. **Flooded Strand's ability** is an activated ability on the stack. Its instruction is: \"Search your library for a Plains or Island card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\"\n\n2. **Gogo, Master of Mimicry's ability** targets that Flooded Strand ability on the stack and, with X=2, creates two copies of it on the stack. Per [Gogo, Master of Mimicry ruling #6], Gogo creates additional instances of the ability; it does not cause any object to gain abilities. Per [707.10b], each copy is itself an ability on the stack, controlled by you, with the same source (Flooded Strand) per [Gogo, Master of Mimicry ruling #9].\n\n3. **Resolving the copies**: Each copy resolves independently. When a copy resolves, it instructs you to search your library for a Plains or Island card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. The original ability also resolves later, doing the same.\n\n4. **Searching multiple times**: Rule [701.23h] states that if an effect instructs a player to search a library more than once before shuffling, it is treated as a single search for all those cards. However, this rule applies only when multiple search instructions occur *before* a single shuffle instruction. Here, each copy (and the original) has its own separate shuffle instruction: \"then shuffle.\" Therefore, each search is a separate event, each followed by its own shuffle. You do not combine the searches into one.\n\n5. **Result**: You resolve the two copies first (in any order you choose), each time searching for a land, putting it onto the battlefield, and shuffling. Then the original ability resolves, letting you search for a third land, put it onto the battlefield, and shuffle. So you get three lands total.\n\n**Key definitions**:\n- **Activated ability**: An ability written as \"[Cost]: [Effect]\" (rule 602). Flooded Strand's ability is an activated ability.\n- **Copy of an ability**: A copy is put onto the stack without being activated; it copies all decisions made for the original, including targets (rule [707.10b]). Since Flooded Strand's ability has no targets, the copies have no targets either.\n- **Search**: Searching a library is a specific action; each search instruction is followed by a shuffle unless otherwise stated (rule [701.23f]).\n\n**Multiplayer/Commander note**: The same logic applies in any game format. Each copy and the original are separate abilities on the stack, each resolving independently with its own search and shuffle. The number of lands you get is always 1 (original) + X (copies from Gogo).",
   "citations": [
    "701.23h",
    "707.10b",
    "Gogo, Master of Mimicry ruling #6",
    "Gogo, Master of Mimicry ruling #9",
    "701.23f"
   ],
   "error": null,
   "raw_text": null
  }
